  "FLINK-33077": {
    "jira_id": "FLINK-33077",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Minimize the risk of hard back-pressure with buffer debloating enabled",
    "description": "{*}Problem{*}:\r\nBuffer debloating sets buffer size to {{256}} bytes because of back-pressure.\r\nSuch small buffers might not be enough to emit the processing results of a single record. The task thread would request new buffers, and often block.\r\nThat results in significant checkpoint delays (up to minutes instead of seconds).\r\n\r\nAdding more overdraft buffers helps, but depends on the job DoP\r\nRaising {{taskmanager.memory.min-segment-size}} from {{256}} helps, but depends on the multiplication factor of the operator.\r\n\r\n{*}Solution{*}:\r\n * Ignore Buffer Debloater hints and extend the buffer if possible - when this prevents emitting an output record fully AND this is the last available buffer.\r\n * Prevent the subsequent flush of the buffer so that more output records can be emitted (flatMap-like and join operators)",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "7aef1fa3a4dabaac14e7fbc1620d4e349b7ac0d4",
        "message": "[FLINK-33077][runtime] Minimize the risk of hard back-pressure with buffer debloating enabled",
        "author": "rkhachatryan",
        "date": "2023-08-11T11:51:07Z",
        "files": [
          {
            "PARENT_PATH": "flink-runtime/src/main/java/org/apache/flink/runtime/io/network/partition/BufferWritingResultPartition.java",
            "CHILD_PATH": "flink-runtime/src/main/java/org/apache/flink/runtime/io/network/partition/BufferWritingResultPartition.java",
            "PATH_CHANGED": false,
